sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    
    participant Client
    participant API as Notification API
    participant Pref as Preference Service
    participant Template as Template Service
    participant Renderer as Renderer
    participant Cache as Redis Cache
    participant Queue as Kafka Queue
    participant Worker as Email Worker
    participant Provider as SendGrid
    participant DB as Cassandra
    participant DLQ as Dead Letter Queue
    
    Note over Client,DLQ: Send Notification Flow
    
    Client->>API: POST /api/v1/notifications<br/>{userId, templateId, channel, variables}
    
    API->>API: Validate request format
    
    API->>Cache: Check idempotency key
    
    alt Already processed
        Cache-->>API: Existing notification ID
        API-->>Client: 200 OK (existing)
    end
    
    API->>Pref: Get user preferences
    Pref->>Cache: Check cache
    
    alt Cache hit
        Cache-->>Pref: Preferences
    else Cache miss
        Pref->>DB: Query preferences
        DB-->>Pref: Preferences
        Pref->>Cache: Store in cache
    end
    
    Pref-->>API: User preferences
    
    alt Channel disabled
        API-->>Client: 200 OK (skipped - opted out)
    end
    
    API->>Template: Get template
    Template->>Cache: Check template cache
    Cache-->>Template: Cached template
    Template-->>API: Template content
    
    API->>Renderer: Render template with variables
    Renderer-->>API: Rendered content
    
    API->>DB: INSERT notification (status: queued)
    DB-->>API: Saved
    
    API->>Cache: SET idempotency key
    
    API->>Queue: Publish to priority queue
    Queue-->>API: Acknowledged
    
    API-->>Client: 202 Accepted<br/>{notificationId, status: "queued"}
    
    Note over Queue,DLQ: Async Worker Processing
    
    Worker->>Queue: Poll messages
    Queue-->>Worker: Notification message
    
    Worker->>Worker: Rate limit check
    
    Worker->>Provider: Send email via API
    
    alt Delivery Success
        Provider-->>Worker: 200 OK {messageId}
        Worker->>DB: UPDATE status = 'sent'
        
        Note over Provider,Worker: Webhook callback later
        Provider-->>Worker: Webhook: delivered
        Worker->>DB: UPDATE status = 'delivered'
        
    else Transient Failure (5xx, timeout)
        Provider-->>Worker: Error
        Worker->>Worker: Check attempt count
        
        alt Attempts < 6
            Worker->>Queue: Requeue with delay<br/>(exponential backoff)
            Worker->>DB: UPDATE attempt_count++
        else Max attempts reached
            Worker->>DLQ: Move to DLQ
            Worker->>DB: UPDATE status = 'failed'
        end
        
    else Permanent Failure (4xx)
        Provider-->>Worker: 400 Bad Request
        Worker->>DLQ: Move to DLQ
        Worker->>DB: UPDATE status = 'failed'
    end
    
    Note over Client,DLQ: Status Check Flow
    
    Client->>API: GET /notifications/{id}/status
    API->>DB: Query notification
    DB-->>API: Notification record
    API-->>Client: {status, deliveredAt, attempts}
